[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":12,"col":10},"end":{"line":12,"col":35}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`List.push` changes `Main.initial.items` in place, but it is `initial`, a\ntop-level value.\n\n12|grow n = List.push initial.items n\n            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n8|initial = { items = [ 7 ] }\n  ^^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nMake `initial` a function that builds a fresh value at each call, or change a\ncopy: `List.copy initial.items`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list (ownership-checker.md §4.2)."}]
